From bd1828a55be328bc144f2ae9523ed9f0ff7dbc5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:00:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Part: volume properties keep the fixed rule on invalid shapes

The adaptive Gauss / Gauss-Kronrod rules added for NURBS accuracy (book ch28) never
finished on an invalid solid such as a box filleted with a radius larger than half its
edge (Part.makeBox(20,20,20).makeFillet(12, edges): official FreeCAD reports a volume
of -8.3e10 in seconds, the patched build hung for more than 15 minutes). An invalid
solid has no meaningful volume; use the bounded fixed-order rule there.
---
 src/Mod/Part/App/TopoShape.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Mod/Part/App/TopoShape.cpp b/src/Mod/Part/App/TopoShape.cpp
index 3990721..fd64716 100644
--- a/src/Mod/Part/App/TopoShape.cpp
+++ b/src/Mod/Part/App/TopoShape.cpp
@@ -1214,7 +1214,10 @@ void TopoShape::volumeProperties(const TopoDS_Shape& shape, GProp_GProps& props,
                 elementary = false;
         }
     }
-    if (elementary) {
+    // An invalid solid (e.g. a fillet the kernel "succeeded" with, volume of the wrong sign or
+    // orders of magnitude off) has no meaningful volume, and the adaptive rules below can refine
+    // forever on it: the GUI hung on such a shape. Keep the fixed rule there (bounded time).
+    if (elementary || !BRepCheck_Analyzer(shape).IsValid()) {
         BRepGProp::VolumeProperties(shape, props);
         return;
     }
